Aim
To simulate an inventory management system using GPSS and study storage handling and customer servicing.

Theory
An Inventory System is used to manage goods, materials, or products stored in a warehouse or shop. 
The main objective of inventory management is to maintain proper stock levels while minimizing shortages and delays.
In this experiment, customers or product requests arrive at the system. If inventory resources are available, the request is processed immediately. Otherwise, the request waits until storage becomes available.
The GENERATE block creates customer requests. The QUEUE block stores requests in the waiting line. 
The ENTER block allows the transaction to enter the storage area if space is available. The LEAVE block releases the storage after processing.
The ADVANCE block represents the processing time for inventory handling.
The STORAGE block defines the total storage capacity available in the system.

Applications:

Warehouse management
Retail inventory systems
Supply chain management
Manufacturing industries
Online shopping systems

Advantages:

Reduces stock shortages
Improves storage management
Helps in planning resources
Increases operational efficiency

Conclusion

Thus, the simulation of an inventory system was successfully performed using GPSS. 
The experiment helped in understanding storage allocation, inventory handling, and processing of requests. The output showed storage utilization and queue statistics.
